        "id": 5680,
        "name": "NDRWnerd",
        "username": "NDRWnerd",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/96bed5/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-28T02:25:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>What’s the reason Spite hurts himself when he becomes a Drug-Wracked Monstrosity for each Victim “saved” by the heroes?</p>\n<p>Is he so crazy that he can’t deal with the fact he didn’t get to kill all those people, so he takes it out on himself (x5) ??<br>\nDoes he somehow need to feed off a humans life-force when he transforms, and if he doesn’t have the victim he burns some of his own life-force?<br>\nPerhaps he goes on a rampage, breaks into the safe-house to kill all the victims, but takes horrible damage in the process (like rampaging through the Rook City Police Department while every cop in town shoots him up).<br>\nOr is &gt;G’s simply teaching us about the perils of drug use, and the damaging effect it has on ourselves and our support netwok of friends and loved ones…</p>\n<p>OK that last one may be a little tongue-in-cheek (though it doesn’t stop me saying it to my group whenever we fight Spite  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=9\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\"> ), but I’d really like to know the rationale for the mechanic.</p>\n<p>edit: I didn’t know whether this would go here in General Discussion or in World.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:24.121Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
