        "id": 29103,
        "name": "EvanDan55",
        "username": "EvanDan55",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/evandan55/{size}/2374_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-28T03:54:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think it’s supposed to be like since Spite needs to kill people to keep himself alive, he’s slowly being hurt, and saving victims prevents him from regenerating, but he gets hurt all at once. So from a story standpoint, whenever you save a victim, Spite is like “Oh crap, I’m dying! I haven’t killed enough!” And when he finally turns into the drug monster, he hasn’t killed as much as he should have been, so the drugs take a serious toll on him.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:03:04.009Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
